 ### [GaussianHead](8051-gaussianhead.md)
-GaussianHead is a method for animatable head reconstruction that uses a tri-plane representation and motion fields to simulate geometrically changing heads in continuous movements. It is designed to render rich textures, including skin and hair. It differs from siblings like GART and D3GA by explicitly leveraging tri-plane features for deformation rather than relying solely on skeleton-based or mesh-based deformation priors.
+GaussianHead reconstructs animatable head avatars by combining a tri-plane representation with motion fields to simulate geometrically changing heads during continuous movements. It renders rich textures, including skin and hair. It builds on the canonical space deformation principles of [Human and Articulated Avatars](8209-human-and-articulated-avatars.md).
 
 ### [GART](8093-gart.md)
-GART is a 3D Gaussian Splatting-based approach designed to animate articulated non-human models, such as animals, by extending the canonical space deformation principles originally developed for human avatars. Unlike sibling methods like [GaussianHead](8051-gaussianhead.md) or [D3GA](8094-d3ga.md) which focus on specific human facial or body parts, GART generalizes the template-guided parameterization to broader articulated skeletons. It solves the problem of realistic, real-time rendering of complex, non-human articulated figures by mapping canonical 3D Gaussians to target poses via a differentiable deformation function.
+GART extends human models to more articulated models based on the 3DGS representation. It builds on [Human and Articulated Avatars](8209-human-and-articulated-avatars.md) [G].
 
 ### [D3GA](8094-d3ga.md)
-D3GA is a method for creating animatable human avatars using drivable 3D Gaussians and tetrahedral cages for full-body modeling. It addresses the challenge of reconstructing dynamic humans from multi-view videos by providing promising geometry and appearance modeling. It sets itself apart from siblings like SplatArmor and HuGS by utilizing tetrahedral cages as the primary deformation structure for the drivable Gaussians.
+D3GA creates animatable human avatars using drivable 3D Gaussians and tetrahedral cages for full-body modeling. It addresses dynamic human reconstruction from multi-view videos by providing promising geometry and appearance modeling. It sets itself apart from head-only siblings like [GaussianHead](8051-gaussianhead.md), [GART](8093-gart.md), and [HeadGas](17293-headgas.md) by extending the drivable Gaussian representation to the full body.
 
